    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Decoherence does not erase every superposition in an arbitrary basis. The system-environment interaction selects comparatively stable pointer states. For pure Z dephasing, those are zero and one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Show how an environment selects a pointer basis.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — OPEN SYSTEMS",
            "segment": "Why This Direction?",
            "greeting": "Merhaba, Liam",
            "runningText": "reading the interaction observable…",
            "output": [
              "Z-type coupling distinguishes |0> from |1>.",
              "Their superpositions lose relative coherence."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.33,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "Use an idealized interaction proportional to sigma Z coupled to an environmental variable. The environment responds differently to the Z eigenstates zero and one.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.41,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "A zero branch becomes correlated with environmental record E zero; a one branch with E one. As those records become distinguishable, their overlap falls.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "split"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.15,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "If the qubit starts in zero or one, pure dephasing leaves its Z population unchanged. These basis states are stable under this interaction, apart from possible phases.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.58,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "If it starts in plus, the two Z branches acquire different environmental records. The relative phase becomes inaccessible locally, and the transverse Bloch vector shrinks toward the center.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.14,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The resulting local mixture is diagonal in the Z basis, not the X basis. The preferred direction came from what the environment could distinguish.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.83,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "But always is too strong. If the coupling monitored X instead, plus and minus would be the stable candidates. More complicated couplings can yield approximate, time-dependent, or competing pointer structures.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.14,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "The system's own Hamiltonian can also compete with environmental monitoring. Pointer states are therefore selected by the full dynamics and timescale hierarchy, not by a basis label chosen in advance.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.31,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "This is environment-induced superselection: robust states persist while coherent combinations of differently recorded states decohere. It explains basis stability, not which unique outcome occurs.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.22,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. A qubit undergoes ideal Z dephasing. Which states are stable, and what happens to plus? Pause before the answer: zero and one are pointer states; plus loses transverse coherence and becomes a local fifty-fifty Z mixture.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: identify the pointer basis for Z dephasing.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Read the Coupling",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the stable-state test…",
            "output": [
              "Stable candidates: |0> and |1>.",
              "|+>: transverse coherence decays; Z populations stay 1/2, 1/2."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.1,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-18T23:50:03"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Why decoherence picks a direction: the interaction records one observable more reliably than its incompatible alternatives.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "fade"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
